{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791649400,"nonce":"clwI8yCQgl0v+fp4ADc3LQEPTrs=","title":"cn number_input and input_otp rebuild around their fields","message":"`number_input` wraps its field and steppers in a `stateful_with_key` with `.deps([state.signal_id()])`, so every value change rebuilds the group to push the formatted value into the field; each stepper is its own `Stateful\u003cButtonState\u003e`. `input_otp` rebuilds its row of slots on its value signal the same way.\n\nSince b4fa30772178cc0a1bf024106d39b01f07b7c43e a text input shows a value written into its data once `refresh_text_input` is called, with no rebuild. So:\n\n- number_input: on a change to the bound `State\u003cf64\u003e`, write the formatted value (and cursor) into the field's data and call `refresh_text_input`; the steppers become `Interaction`-styled buttons like the rest of cn.\n- input_otp: write each slot's character into its data and refresh it, instead of rebuilding the row.\n\nThen neither queues a subtree rebuild; add in-place tests that assert so, as the other cn components have.","files":null}]}